"w79xs6z9cx2m": {
"body": "Between approximately 2026-07-24 03:39\u201305:00 PT (10:39\u201312:00 UTC), some customers may have experienced intermittent connectivity issues while accessing Amplitude or sending data, including connection timeouts. This was caused by an AWS networking disruption in the us-west-2 region affecting multiple upstream AWS services.\n\nThe issue originated outside of Amplitude's infrastructure and was resolved by AWS.\n\nServices:\n- Our SDKs queue undelivered events on-device and automatically retry sending them, so we expect minimal to no data loss from this incident.  No ingested data was lost and no action is required.\n- Experiment/Flag evaluations failed and return 503s due to service unavailability. There is no data loss.",
"first_seen": "2026-09-04T07:06:16Z",
"impact": "none",
"last_seen": "2026-09-04T09:06:33Z",
